# Which parishes the FamilySearch RECORD INDEX covers, and for which events.
#
# Why this file exists. The index-with-ARK method returns the image ARK of every
# indexed entry, so an indexed record opens at the page in one step instead of
# being hunted down a film. It closed three work-list rows in minutes on 15
# September 2026 — and was completely useless for a fourth, because Selce turns
# out to be indexed for baptisms only. Nobody had written that down, so every
# sitting rediscovered it, and row 23 of the work list was written on the wrong
# assumption before this file existed.
#
# Method: /service/search/hr/v2/personas?f.collectionId=2040054&q.surname=<name>,
# several hundred results per surname across eight surnames of this family,
# tallied by place string and event type. Counts are a sample, not a census — the
# point is which event types appear AT ALL, because a zero is the finding.
#
# parish|baptisms|deaths|verdict
Otocac|165|0|BAPTISMS ONLY - not one death or burial in the sample
Selce|77|0|BAPTISMS ONLY - confirmed twice; 119 Antic entries, every one a baptism
Karlobag|yes|0|BAPTISMS ONLY - four surnames tested (Pilipic, Gerkacs, Luckinic, Smojver), every Karlobag hit a baptism, range 1717-1861
Krmpote-Vodice|9|0|BAPTISMS ONLY in the sample
Senj|18+13 birth|8 death + 14 burial|DEATHS ARE INDEXED - also under the Latin place string "Senia" (14 birth, 14 burial, 11 death)
Krivi Put|12+9 birth|11 death + 10 burial|DEATHS ARE INDEXED
Novi Vinodolski|6+7 birth|4 death|DEATHS ARE INDEXED
Crikvenica|6+7 birth|1 death + 3 burial|DEATHS ARE INDEXED, thinly
